    "grammar": [
      "Fixed Panda at 10 Hz, horizon 150, 40mm cubes; speed <=0.1 m/s; five ordered skills approach, align_behind, contact, push_toward, settle. Skill timeouts sum <=150. Teacher references the requested cube and destination in every skill.",
      "Scene schema_version astrapush-1. One red or blue cube + one target for S1. Exactly one red and one blue cube + left/right targets for S2. Two same-color cubes, marker, left/right targets for S3. At most one optional reference_fixture in addition to marker. No obstacles, grasping, new assets, rewards, or executable code.",
      "Cube placement half_width 0.03-0.05m. Target half_width 0.04-0.06m. All axis-aligned square region pairs including fixtures (halfwidth .02m) must be disjoint: in at least one axis, abs(center difference)>=sum halfwidths. |x|+half<=.28, |y|+half<=.32.",
      "Left is smaller table Y. In S3 entire left placement region <= markerY-.05 and right region >= markerY+.05. Marker/fixtures must clear the direct push corridor by >.0483m; preserved other cube region must clear it by >sqrt(2)*(placement_half_width+.02).",
      "Nominal selected cube center to selected target center must be .05-.15m. Keep modest straight, reachable pushes, with enough horizon for approach, lowering, contact, push and >=13 settle commands. Random reset samples inside authored placement regions; each seed may fail and is counted.",
      "Trusted exact instruction grammar: S1 Push the block into the target. S2 Push the {red|blue} block to the {left|right} target. Leave the {other color} block in place. S3 Push the block {left|right} of the marker to the {left|right} target. Leave the other block in place.",
      "TaskProposal has task_id, referent, destination, instruction. Do NOT invent scene_hash; local compiler binds it. Use schema exactly, no extra fields. Choose meaningful layout/composition changes, not IDs or recoloring alone.",
      "Respond with one JSON object under 8192 tokens and 32768 UTF-8 bytes; no markdown. This interface lacks a hard token-cap/usage receipt and is documented as a new transport pilot."
